{"claims":[{"claim_text":"Since 2001, the Democratic Socialists of America national organization has focused political work on combating global capitalism’s ‘race-to-the-bottom’ development strategy.", "claim_types":["factual_assertion"],"evidence_ids":[1]},{"claim_text":"The Democratic Socialists of America asserts that the ‘Walmart-ization’ of the global economy has depressed the quality of life of the world’s working people, including those residing in the United States.", "claim_types":["factual_assertion"],"evidence_ids":[1]},{"claim_text":"The Democratic Socialists of America has engaged in public political education aimed at illustrating that ‘Walmart-ization’ is not caused by the actions of one particular rapacious corporation but by a systemic and irrational model of global capitalist development.", "claim_types":["factual_assertion"],"evidence_ids":[1]},{"claim_text":"The Democratic Socialists of America has highlighted local, national, and transnational efforts to construct an alternative model of fair trade, global labor and human rights, and equitable development strategies.", "claim_types":["factual_assertion"],"evidence_ids":[1]},{"claim_text":"This convention endorses a continuation and deepening of the organizational focus and coordinated activism that the “Low Wage Justice” campaign has brought to the organization.", "claim_types":["policy_position"],"evidence_ids":[1]},{"claim_text":"This convention commits itself to the Democratic Socialists of America National Political Committee and national office continuing to provide resources and information to aid locals in living wage campaigns, immigrant justice activism, and labor support work.", "claim_types":["policy_position"],"evidence_ids":[1]}],"unresolved_references":[]}
```

